Overlay patch 0012: the iOS app target in Starship's CMakeLists (reference/
2ship 0004 template) + new file ios/Info.plist.in.
Upstream HAS an if(IOS) path, but it is bit-rotted at this pin: it hardcodes
PLATFORM=OS64 (breaking simulator builds), includes its own ios.toolchain,
sets a placeholder team id, and references libultraship/ios/{Launch.storyboard,
plist.in,...} which do not exist in the pinned LUS. Replace both blocks:
- top if(IOS): keep PLATFORM_IOS=1 (Game.cpp's extern "C" main gate), enable
  OBJC (the app shell is .m), drop the toolchain include / OS64 / team id.
- add_executable branch: shell wiring (SOH_IOS_SHELL_DIR), __IOS__ PRIVATE on
  the game target (reference D4), bundled starship.o2r + gamecontrollerdb.txt,
  Info.plist.in, INSTALL_PATH/SKIP_INSTALL (2ship OTA lesson), explicit
  UniformTypeIdentifiers + GameController frameworks (2ship autolink lesson).
- audio deps: iOS branch with prebuilt static ogg/vorbis (SOH_IOS_DEPS_PREFIX)
  + SDL2-static/SDL2main from LUS's FetchContent.
- torch gets __IOS__ too (D4).
config.yml + assets/yaml self-bundle via upstream's existing POST_BUILD copy
to $<TARGET_FILE_DIR:Starship> (= .app root on iOS) — the extractor manifests
requirement from docs/asset-pipeline.md.
SOH_* variable names kept reference-verbatim for script/harbour-shell
uniformity.

